# React Runtime - Browser Hot Path

## Status

Applies when `web/src/pages` and `web/src/ui` exist (`ui.mdc`, `frontend-modular.mdc`). Layout and cold-path contracts: `ui.mdc`. Modular boundaries: `frontend-modular.mdc`.

## Purpose

Maps tracker ingest discipline (`hot-path.mdc`) to **V8 + React 19** in the admin SPA. Tracker optimizes **0 allocs/op** on `/track`; admin UI optimizes **low allocation rate per frame** and **bounded reconciliation** on list surfaces.

## Hot vs cold UI surfaces

| Surface | Hot rules apply | Budget |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Data grid scroll / sort / page change | Yes | < 16 ms/frame during scroll |
| Filter keystroke (server refetch) | Yes (debounced) | Spike on Apply only, not per key |
| 1 Hz freshness ticker | Yes (isolated leaf) | Must not commit whole page |
| Chart tick / resize | Yes (imperative lib) | React owns container only |
| Detail form PATCH | Cold | Normal React patterns OK |
| One-off settings pages | Cold | No SoA required |

**List pages with 500+ rows** (or 50+ visible without windowing) follow all sections below.

## Go hot path parity (mental model)

| Go ingest (`hot-path.mdc`) | Browser admin (`react.mdc`) |
| :--- | :--- |
| `atomic.Pointer` catalog snapshot | Immutable fetch snapshot in state; replace whole `data`, do not mutate DTO in place |
| SoA parallel slices (`CampaignIDs`, `Bids`, …) | Parallel arrays or `Map<id, display>` built once in `useMemo` |
| `sync.Pool` reuse | Module-scope constants; reuse `TypedArray` in workers; no per-row object spread |
| Zero `interface{}` / no `fmt.Sprintf` in loop | No inline `style={{}}`, no object-form `cn()`, no template concat in row loop |
| `TryReserve` before debit | Debounce/prefetch before refetch; abort stale fetch before `setState` |
| Pinned worker, no block on Redis | `requestAnimationFrame` coalesce scroll; JSON parse in Worker for large payloads |
| Bench: 0 allocs/op | Profiler: allocation spike on page change only, not per scroll frame |
| Fail closed on miswire | `ErrorBlock` on fetch fail; no silent empty table (`ui.mdc`) |

## Runtime model (V8)

V8 **Orinoco** generational GC: short-lived objects die in nursery (minor GC / Scavenge); survivors promote to old space; major GC reclaims old space when heuristics fire.

| Fact | UI implication |
| :--- | :--- |
| Allocation rate drives jank | Treat **objects per frame** like Go **allocs/op** — minimize in scroll/filter paths |
| No manual `free()` | Reduce churn; reuse refs; drop unreachable graphs (listeners, closures over `items[]`) |
| Hidden classes (maps) | Stable object shapes; same key order on DTOs; never `delete obj.k` on hot rows |
| Immutable strings | Format once in `useMemo`; server sends `*_display` when possible (`ui.mdc`) |
| `map`/`filter`/`flatMap` allocate | One pass in `useMemo` when client slice needed; prefer **server page** over client full-list ops |

No `GOGC` in the browser. Levers: **allocation rate**, **retained graph size**, **React commit count**.

## Interaction budgets (admin UI)

| Surface | Target | Knob |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Keystroke filter | Perceived < 50 ms | Debounce 150–300 ms; server refetch on Apply |
| Data grid scroll | < 16 ms/frame (60 Hz) | Row windowing; `passive` scroll listener; no layout read in handler |
| Sort / page change | One commit for visible window | Server sort; or single `useMemo` slice |
| 1 Hz ticker | No full-page commit | Leaf `memo` + local `useState` |
| Chart update | No React series rebuild | uPlot/ECharts `setData` in place |
| Large JSON (> 256 KiB) | Main thread stays interactive | `web/src/workers/parse_json.worker.ts` |

## Data-oriented design (DoD)

Hot path favors **flat homogeneous columns, snapshot readers, and indexes** over pointer graphs and per-row object factories. Same spirit as `catalogSnapshot` SoA in `internal/rtb/catalog_shard.go` (`hot-path.mdc`).

### Snapshot reader (immutable swap)

```
Fetch completes
  -> setState(nextSnapshot)   // replace reference, never mutate prev.items[i]
  -> useMemo derives view from snapshot + UI primitives (page, sort key)
  -> render reads snapshot + derived columns only
```

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| One writer | Only fetch handler / effect replaces snapshot |
| No in-place row patch | `items[i].status = x` breaks `memo` and hidden classes |
| Generation id | Increment on fetch; ignore stale responses before `setState` |
| Server labels | Prefer `status_label`, `balance_display` from API — less format alloc |

### Array of structs vs structure of arrays (AoS vs SoA)

**AoS** (default API): `items: CustomerDTO[]` — fine when **visible row count is small** (< 50) and fields are read once per row.

**SoA** (homogeneous columns): when one grid renders the same 6–12 fields for hundreds of rows and formats repeat every render.

| AoS (avoid in hot grid) | SoA / parallel (prefer) |
| :--- | :--- |
| `rows.map(r => formatMoney(r.balance))` each render | `useMemo`: `balanceDisplay: string[]` aligned by index |
| `selectedIds.includes(id)` per row O(n) | `Set<string>` built once when selection changes |
| Row receives whole DTO + 3 formatters | Row receives `id`, `name`, `balanceDisplay`, `statusLabel` primitives |
| Nested `items.map` inside cell | Precomputed `Map<parentId, childIds[]>` |

Example (conceptual):

```ts
// Built once when snapshot changes — not inside rows.map
const rowView = useMemo(() => {
  const n = items.length;
  const ids = new Array<string>(n);
  const names = new Array<string>(n);
  const balances = new Array<string>(n);
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    ids[i] = items[i].id;
    names[i] = items[i].name ?? '';
    balances[i] = items[i].balance_display ?? '-';
  }
  return { ids, names, balances, len: n };
}, [items]);
```

Use SoA when Profiler shows **Scripting** scales with row count during scroll. Otherwise server pagination + primitives per row is enough.

### Windowing (scan cap)

Go RTB caps candidates scanned (p99 < 500). Grids cap **DOM nodes + React fibers**:

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Visible window | Render `start..start+windowSize` only; spacer rows for scroll height |
| Stable `key` | `row.id` — never index-only on sorted lists |
| Overscan | +3–5 rows above/below viewport — trade memory for scroll smoothness |
| Full list client sort | **Banned** on large N — server sort + page (`ui.mdc`) |

### Indexes (O(1) lookup)

| Need | Structure |
| :--- | :--- |
| Row by id | `Map<string, CustomerDTO>` once per snapshot |
| Selected set | `Set<string>` |
| Group children | `Map<string, string[]>` built in one pass |
| Text search (client, small N only) | Inverted index in `useMemo` — not `.includes` per row per render |

## Prefetch and decode

Analog to **warm catalog before auction** and **reserve before debit** — hide latency without allocating on the scroll hot path.

### Fetch prefetch

| Pattern | When |
| :--- | :--- |
| Next page prefetch | After page N renders, `idleCallback` or `setTimeout(0)` fetch page N+1 with same filters; store in ref, commit on "Next" |
| Route prefetch | On nav item `mouseenter`, dynamic `import()` of page chunk only — not data until route active |
| Stale-while-revalidate | Keep previous `data` visible while refetching; toast on error (`ui.mdc`) |
| Abort | New params -> `AbortController.abort()`; do not stack in-flight lists |

```ts
// Prefetch: ref only — no setState until user advances page
const prefetchRef = useRef<CustomerListResponse | null>(null);

useEffect(() => {
  if (!hasNextPage) return;
  const ctrl = new AbortController();
  const run = () => {
    void listCustomers({ ...params, offset: params.offset + params.limit }, ctrl.signal)
      .then((res) => { prefetchRef.current = res; })
      .catch(() => {});
  };
  const id = requestIdleCallback?.(run) ?? window.setTimeout(run, 200);
  return () => {
    ctrl.abort();
    if (typeof id === 'number') clearTimeout(id);
    else cancelIdleCallback(id);
  };
}, [params, hasNextPage]);
```

### Worker offload

| Workload | Thread |
| :--- | :--- |
| `JSON.parse` on large list payloads | `parse_json.worker.ts` |
| CSV / aggregate report post-process | `report_aggregate.worker.ts` |
| Small `< 64 KiB` responses | Main thread `api()` is fine |

Worker rules:

- Transferable buffers when possible (`postMessage(buf, [buf])`) to avoid copy alloc on main thread.
- One long-lived worker per page session; `terminate()` on unmount.
- Parsed result still replaces snapshot once — no per-row postMessage.

### Debounce and coalescing

| Input | Pattern |
| :--- | :--- |
| Search field | Debounce 150–300 ms before server refetch |
| Scroll sync | `requestAnimationFrame` flag — one layout read per frame |
| Resize | rAF-debounced `ResizeObserver` callback |

## Hot render path (forbidden)

Inside `rows.map`, scroll handlers, filter handlers, chart ticks:

| Category | Forbidden |
| :--- | :--- |
| Alloc per row | `rows.map(r => ({ ...r, label: format(r) }))` |
| O(n²) | `.find` / `.filter` inside cell render; nested full-dataset `map` |
| Fresh objects | Inline `style={{}}`; object-form `cn()` every row |
| Fresh functions | Inline `onClick={() => ...}` on `memo` rows without stable handler |
| JSON | `JSON.parse` / `stringify` in render |
| Client sort/filter | Full `items[]` sort/filter without `useMemo` or server params |
| Context broadcast | 1 Hz `now`, scroll offset, mouse position at page root |
| Intervals | `setInterval` on page parent |
| DOM retention | `document` listeners without cleanup; closure over full `items[]` |
| Spread churn | `{...prev, ...patch}` on large state each keystroke |
| Layout thrash | `getBoundingClientRect` per row in scroll handler |

## Allowed patterns

| Pattern | Usage |
| :--- | :--- |
| Snapshot state | Fetch once; derive in `useMemo` |
| SoA columns | Parallel string arrays for display fields |
| `Map` / `Set` indexes | Selection, lookup — built when snapshot changes |
| Colocated state | Dropdown open, hover in leaf component |
| `useRef` | Prefetch cache, generation id, abort controller |
| `memo` + stable props | Rows when visible count > ~50 |
| `useCallback` | Stable handlers for `memo` children only |
| `useMemo` | Column defs, SoA build, page slice (if client windowed) |
| Debounce / rAF | Search, scroll, resize |
| Abort + generation | Ignore stale fetch before `setState` |
| Imperative charts | Chart lib mutates buffers; React holds `div` ref |
| `WeakMap` | Optional cache keyed by row identity — not correctness |

## State shape

**Cold snapshot + derived view** — same as `atomic.Pointer` swap in Go.

```
Server snapshot (useState / useResource)
  -> useMemo: rowView (SoA) or pageItems (slice)
  -> render: windowed map(Row)
```

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| One source of truth | API DTO in `data`; UI toggles separate primitives |
| Draft vs applied | Filter draft local; Apply copies to URL params once |
| Minimal lift | Share only what siblings need |
| URL sync | On Apply / page change — not every keystroke |
| Error | Single `error` object; explicit branches (`ui.mdc`) |

Forbidden: giant spread state; duplicated row arrays in state; formatted strings in state when derivable in `useMemo`.

## Closures and retention (heap leaks)

| Leak | Fix |
| :--- | :--- |
| `setInterval` without cleanup | `return () => clearInterval(t)` |
| `document.addEventListener` | Remove in effect cleanup |
| Fetch after unmount | `AbortController` + generation check |
| Closure over `items` in timer | `itemsRef.current = items` |
| Portal menu left mounted | Unmount on close |
| Unbounded module `Map` cache | Cap or `WeakMap` |

`WeakRef` / `FinalizationRegistry`: optional caches only.

## Effects and subscriptions

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| One concern per effect | fetch / subscribe / URL sync |
| Minimal deps | Refs for values that must not retrigger |
| Strict Mode | Cleanup idempotent |
| Fetch | `useResource` or effect + abort — never in render |
| Poll | Single effect; push snapshot, not per-tick spread of list |

## React reconciliation

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Split trees | Ticker sibling to grid — not child |
| Context split | Auth / theme / data separate |
| `key` | Stable `row.id` |
| `memo` | Row when parent hot, props stable |
| `children` | No inline `<Heavy />` on hot parent |

React Compiler does not remove GC pressure from new arrays.

## V8-friendly habits

| Habit | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Module-scope options | `const STATUS_OPTIONS = [...] as const` |
| Column defs at module scope | `as const` tuples |
| Avoid `delete` on DTOs | Treat API objects as read-only |
| `cn()` in row loop | String args only |
| Hidden class stability | Same fields on each row object from API |

## Charts and canvas

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Ownership | React: container + resize observer |
| Update | `setOption` / `setData` in place |
| Unmount | `dispose()` in cleanup |
| Resize | rAF-debounced; one `getBoundingClientRect` per frame |

## Verification

| Step | Command / tool |
| :--- | :--- |
| Types | `cd web && npm run typecheck` |
| UI gates | `bash scripts/ci/check_ui_surface_gate.sh` && `bash scripts/ci/admin_web.sh` |
| React Profiler | 500-row fixture: scroll + sort — page chrome not in every commit |
| Performance (6x slowdown) | **Scripting** + **GC** during scroll — GC bar should not track scroll frame-by-frame |
| Allocation sampling | Filter: spike on Apply only |
| Memory | 10 navigate cycles — detached nodes stable |
| Honesty | Admin microbench ≠ tracker p99 (`anti-slop.mdc`) |

Before claiming list perf: paste Profiler note or row window size + visible count.

## Agent checklist

| Step | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| 1 | Server pagination/sort when N > 100 |
| 2 | Snapshot replace; SoA or primitives for hot grids |
| 3 | Prefetch next page in ref; abort stale fetches |
| 4 | Ticker isolated in `memo` leaf |
| 5 | Large JSON -> worker parse |
| 6 | Profiler check on changed list page |

